# Companion OS: apt must never swap the initramfs generator of this system.
#
# The stock Ubuntu 26.04 desktop image installs dracut (it Conflicts with initramfs-tools). Its live layer swaps dracut out
# for initramfs-tools, and the base image Companion OS installs from is the live system's view of it: an initramfs-tools
# system (casper needs that generator, and so does the install-time update-initramfs the installer runs). ubuntu-desktop-minimal
# Recommends dracut, so without this file a later `apt install` or upgrade could pull dracut back in and remove
# initramfs-tools, and the next kernel update would build a different kind of initrd than the one that was tested.
#
# Priority -1 means "never install". Only the generator itself is pinned: dracut and dracut-core. dracut-install is
# NOT: it is a helper that initramfs-tools-core depends on, so pinning it would freeze it at the installed version and
# keep its security updates out (measured with `apt-get -s dist-upgrade` on 26.04).
Package: dracut dracut-core
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1
